<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polish–Teutonic War (1326–1332)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1326">1326</a>–<a href="/years/1332">1332</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polish–Teutonic War of 1326–1332 was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> under Władysław I the Elbow-high and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerelia">Pomerelia</a>, which the knights had seized in 1308. The Order, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-bohemia">John of Bohemia</a>, invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuyavia">Kuyavia</a> and Greater <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poles">Poles</a> fought it to a draw at Płowce in 1331. It ended with a truce in 1332 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kalisz-1343">Treaty of Kalisz</a> in 1343.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polish-teutonic-war-1326-1332.jpg" alt="Polish–Teutonic War (1326–1332)" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dr. Karl von Spruner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Central_Europe_in_the_early_14th_century..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
